Trance Syndicate ✦ 1998

Steve Albini, on recording the underappreciated Texas slowcore band’s final record: “No detail was too small to sweat, no crack in the veneer not worth gluing and clamping. We built a common language, equal parts philosophy, rock music, and disdain for the dullness around us.” Slow tempos, ominous lyrics, some guitar solos, maximum impact. Light a candle and listen, knowing that the band never recorded alternate takes in the studio; they just kept recording over the old ones until it was perfect. –Jeremy D. Larson

