Here’s a question that you might overhear after a couple beers at a Boston bar: Where does Western Massachusetts, the region of small towns, art museums, and former industrial hubs a couple hours’ drive from the city, actually begin? One common answer is just past the Quabbin Reservoir, a vast body of water said to be haunted by the ghost towns it engulfed. My mind, and probably yours, immediately goes to Amherst, home of Dinosaur Jr., the greatest band to ever come of the region. Their story of genre-defining records and quarrelling members has been told over and over, with [new wrinkles each time](https://pitchfork.com/story/how-dinosaur-jr-learned-to-tolerate-one-another-kind-of/). We have our squabbles with coworkers, and still we go to work.

